## Layout & Spacing Guidelines

These utility classes are automatically generated from the SCSS configuration and are used to manage **layout, spacing, and alignment** throughout the application.

All classes follow the prefix **`ft-`**, and their values are based on the design tokens defined in `variables-scss`.

---

### Responsive Breakpoints

Most layout and display utilities support **responsive variants** for the following breakpoints:

| Breakpoint | Suffix | Example usage              |
|-------------|---------|----------------------------|
| Extra small | `xs`    | `ft-d-xs-f`             |
| Small       | `sm`    | `ft-jc-sm-c`          |
| Medium      | `md`    | `ft-d-md-g`             |
| Large       | `lg`    | `ft-ai-lg-c`          |
| Extra large | `xl`    | `ft-fd-xl-c`          |
| 2× Extra large | `xxl` | `ft-d-xxl-n`           |

Example:

```html
<div class="ft-d-f ft-d-md-b ft-jc-lg-c">
  ...
</div>

### Gap Utilities

Control spacing between elements in flex or grid layouts.

| Property      | Class Prefix | Example        | Description                        |
|----------------|---------------|----------------|------------------------------------|
| `gap`          | `ft-g`        | `ft-g-2`       | Sets uniform gap between elements. |
| `column-gap`   | `ft-cg`       | `ft-cg-3`      | Controls horizontal gap.           |
| `row-gap`      | `ft-rg`       | `ft-rg-1`      | Controls vertical gap.             |

---

### Padding Utilities

Use padding classes to control internal spacing.

| Property               | Class Prefix | Example        | Description |
|--------------------------|--------------|----------------|--------------|
| `padding`               | `ft-p`       | `ft-p-2`       | All sides padding. |
| `padding-block`         | `ft-pb`      | `ft-pb-1`      | Top & bottom padding. |
| `padding-block-start`   | `ft-pbs`     | `ft-pbs-3`     | Top padding only. |
| `padding-block-end`     | `ft-pbe`     | `ft-pbe-1`     | Bottom padding only. |
| `padding-inline`        | `ft-pi`      | `ft-pi-4`      | Left & right padding. |
| `padding-inline-start`  | `ft-pis`     | `ft-pis-2`     | Left padding only. |
| `padding-inline-end`    | `ft-pie`     | `ft-pie-2`     | Right padding only. |

---

### Margin Utilities

Similar to padding utilities but for external spacing.

| Property               | Class Prefix | Example        | Description |
|--------------------------|--------------|----------------|--------------|
| `margin`               | `ft-m`       | `ft-m-2`       | All sides margin. |
| `margin-block`         | `ft-mb`      | `ft-mb-1`      | Top & bottom margin. |
| `margin-block-start`   | `ft-mbs`     | `ft-mbs-3`     | Top margin only. |
| `margin-block-end`     | `ft-mbe`     | `ft-mbe-1`     | Bottom margin only. |
| `margin-inline`        | `ft-mi`      | `ft-mi-2`      | Left & right margin. |
| `margin-inline-start`  | `ft-mis`     | `ft-mis-2`     | Left margin only. |
| `margin-inline-end`    | `ft-mie`     | `ft-mie-2`     | Right margin only. |

💡 You can also use **`auto`** values where supported, e.g.:
```html
<div class="ft-mi-auto">...</div>

### Width Utilities

| Class       | Description             |
|--------------|-------------------------|
| `ft-w-100`   | Forces width to 100%.   |
| `ft-h-100`   | Forces height to 100%.   |

### General Rules

- Use layout utilities instead of custom CSS whenever possible.
- Keep class combinations minimal and semantic.
- Combine gap, padding, and margin utilities for consistent spacing control.
- Always prefer the responsive variants (-xs, -sm, -md, -lg, -xl, -xxl) when needed for adaptive layouts.
- Maintain consistency with existing design tokens and spacing scale.